// #load is a declaration of the program's (issue #112): not in a body. The
// file it names isn't loaded: it declares main, which would be declared
// twice if it were. The program then lacks that file, so greet, which it
// declares, isn't reported as unknown too: the one mistake is said once.
main :: () {
    #load "load/other_main.rig";
    greet();
}
